# PIPELINE 3 — AORTIC STENOSIS (AS) DATASET

# Three contrasts from one model:
#   1. TGFB1_DMSO vs SF_DMSO_citric
#      Baseline: TGF-B1 effect on AV tissue
#   2. TGFB1_Nintedanib vs TGFB1_DMSO
#      Nintedanib treatment effect
#   3. TGFB1_Senicapoc vs TGFB1_DMSO
#      Senicapoc treatment effect

# All objects are prefixed P3_ to avoid conflicts with Pipeline 2.

# IMPORTANT:
# AS samples are single technical replicates!! not triplicates like IPF & healthy lung tissue
# Each donor contributes ONLY ONE measurement per condition.

# Consequences:
#   - Imputed values carry higher uncertainty than replicated datasets.
#   - ARSyNseq donor-effect estimates are based on single measurements.
#   - Robust empirical Bayes moderation is used to reduce sensitivity to
#     outlier variance.
#   - Drug contrasts are exploratory.
#   - Drug-contrast results are interpreted using nominal p < 0.05 because
#     no proteins survive FDR correction.

#NOTE: though fundamentally simailr, this pipeline includes a few key differences to
      #account for limitations of this dataset!
##############################################################

